A||N||16||Monkeyman||Where's the trunk light switch?||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||09-15-2001||09:55 PM||||My trunk rear trunk light refuses to turn off so I bought a new switch (the one that the decklid hits and depresses) figuring that was probably the problem (at least it was on the last 3 Fieros).  Only problem now is that I can't find the thing.  Where is it located on an '86 GT?  I looked all over but I can't even see where there is a hole for one (can't see any loose wires that would go to it, either).||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ronnie||09-15-2001||10:14 PM||||Monkeyman , the switch is on the latch itself on the decklid. Look at the latch , it's a little fingerlike thing.||||reg||6
Z||000002||Phil||09-15-2001||10:14 PM||||I don't know what year they changed but my 88's all have the switch in the latch itself(little black flippy lever).||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ronnie||09-15-2001||10:16 PM||||It's me again!! If you can't find it there , could be yours is broke off , which would make the light stay on all the time.||||reg||6
Z||000004||Monkeyman||09-15-2001||10:19 PM||||Thanx.  I'll have to look tomorrow in the daylight.  They must have changed in '86 but only in some models.  The Monkeymobile ('86 coupe still uses the plunger type as did both of my '85 GTs.<P>Does the flippy thing break often and is there anyone who sells replacements?  I have no idea what could be wrong.  My trunk light just won't turn off.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>In memory of those that died on 11 Sept 2001.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1367.gif">  <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||09-15-2001||10:33 PM||||Curiosity got the best of me so I went out to look.  I can't find it anywhere.  The only wires I see are for the remote decklid release (small ground wire on the left side and small wiring harness on the right).  I don't see any other wiring that goes either to the decklid or around it.  The trunk light must be standard on my car as I have the hole in the trunk for the light and the wiring to that.<P>Where exactly is this switch and what does it look like?  A pic might help.<P>------------------<BR>In memory of those that died on 11 Sept 2001.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1367.gif">  <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ronnie||09-15-2001||10:38 PM||||Well , my 86 & 88 GT's have it located there , but the 88 Formula doesn't have a trunk light. So , maybe the GT's are different? I don't know.||||reg||6
Z||000007||Fformula88||09-15-2001||11:10 PM||||My 88 has it on the decklid bracket too, but I don't have the remote release.  Maybe its set up differently with that option.  The 85 SE isn't here (its in our rented garage) so I cannot look at where it is in that car.<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000008||jelly2m8||09-16-2001||12:07 AM||||84's and 85's have the switch mounted on the lip of the trunk opening , in the engine bay, to the left. Its a pin switch like the front compartment, and door light switch. <P>86 and up have the switch in the deck latch, it has a black lever, and is mounted on the facing side of the latch||||reg||1
Z||000009||Spiff||09-16-2001||12:13 AM||||Speaking of the trunk light. My Formula does not have one. Is there a way to install one?||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||09-16-2001||12:27 AM||||look at the right hinge area. 86's I've seen have the wires there. I beleive it was an 86, maybe an 86.5, that coughed up the wire, etc, I used to add the power release to my trunk. (article in cave...)<P>The switch is on the latch itself. 3 wires go to the switch. the 4<sup>th</sup> wire, if present goes to the release solinoid.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000011||JohnF||09-16-2001||08:04 AM||||For a 1988 coupe, can someone with a trunk AJAR swith intact please post a photo of it installed.  Mine is broken off and I would like to repair/reinstall.||||reg||5
Z||000012||Mickey_Moose||09-16-2001||10:25 AM||||switch &gt;&gt; on a 88 (seen this on other years), the switch for the trunk lamp is located on the rear deck lid. As you open the cover and look directly at the latch, the switch is the first thing you see (it's bolted with 2 machine screws to the latch assembly - ie. closer to the rear of the car than the latch)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>sorry no picture, but hope that helps.<P>ps &gt;&gt; the wiring harness/plug is located (looking from the rear to the front of the car) on the right lid hinge on the inside side of it. There is a ground wire on the left side as well which bolts to the deck lid.<P>Tim<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000013||Monkeyman||09-16-2001||03:09 PM||||I found something on the trunk latch.  Now I can't get any power to the trunk light at all.  This is crazy.  I guess I don't really need a trunk light anyway.  That's what a flash light is for, right?<P>------------------<BR>In memory of those that died on 11 Sept 2001.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1367.gif">  <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||1
Z||000014||theogre||09-16-2001||03:26 PM||||Trunk switch is on the latch. You need to take the latch off the lid to replace it. Mark the latch location before removal so you can put it back the way it was. There is a harness connector hidden under the latch for the switch. If you mark the original location it won't take but a few minutes to change the switch.<P>Check the harness and connectore where the wire exits the lid by the right hinge. That connector is suposed to clip to the framing the hinge is bolted to. The clip breaks then the thing melts on the manifold or, on the 4 cyl, get's eaten by the fan belt. <P>The switch provides a ground path for the ajar and trunk light. The power release, if present, grounds thru the latch strike.<P>If the fuse was out then the power release wouldn't work either. The trunk release and light are both on the ctsy/lid fuse.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Monkeyman||09-16-2001||04:04 PM||||Maybe I'm getting a little confused now.  Here's what I know.  When I bought the car, the trunk light was blown.  I swapped bulbs and the light worked.  Unfortunately, it wouldn't turn off and I drained my battery.  I found (I think) the trunk light switch on the trunk latch (black thing towards the back edge of the latch?).  I plugged in the good bulb, and...nothing.  I jiggled the switch around and still nothing.  The wiring harness that enters the decklid at the right side hinge is fine.  The remote decklid release works fine, too.<P>Here's another (possibly related) lighting problem.  The front light doesn't seem to work, either.  It looks like it has a good bulb and I tried to check it with a test light (doesn't seem to have any power).  I tried it with:  no lights on, parking only lights on and headlights on.  Still nothing.  Is there a common fuse for both trunk lights (front and back)?  If it's the fuse and I can get both to work, I'm still back to square one, but at least I'm in better shape than I'm in now.<P>Once I get the lights to come on, is there a reason why the rear light wouldn't go out?<P>Sorry for the bandwidth.<P>------------------<BR>In memory of those that died on 11 Sept 2001.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1367.gif">  <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||1
Z||000016||theogre||09-16-2001||05:52 PM||||The black thing on the decklatch is the switch. A bad switch could kill it or keep it on. If you are carefull you can change it w/o removing the latch. Make sure you don't let the connector drop into the trunk...<P>Unplug the switch and set it asside.<P>The black wire on the switch connector is ground. Connecting between it and the white wire turns on the trunk light. black to green turns on ajar if the key is on.<P>Also both the switch connector and C250 by the hinge are lettered. It's molded right into the shell. Fortunatly the lettering is the same on both.<P>A, Ajar, Dark Green<BR>B, Trunk light, white or white orange depending on which connector you are holding.<BR>C, Ground, black<BR>D, black/white, on C250 is the power release solinoid. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-16-2001).]||||reg||1
